<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	xmlns:vc="http://www.w3.org/2007/XMLSchema-versioning"
	vc:minVersion="1.1"
	elementFormDefault="qualified"
	attributeFormDefault="unqualified"
	xmlns="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p500#"
	xmlns:tns="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p500#"
	targetNamespace="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p500#"
	>

	<xs:include schemaLocation="P500_Series_Common.xsd"/>

	<xs:annotation>
		<xs:documentation>
			NAS9300 500-series ARCHIVE MANIFEST — the top-level manifest of a single 500-series
			archive (one OAIS AIP holding all 5xx artifacts of one configured baseline), and the
			record format of the metadata-only BASELINE LINK ARCHIVE that relates archives of
			different series.

			Status: DRAFT supplied by the NAS9300-520 drafting team as the first working instance
			(D-25, 2026-10-28, executing WG decisions S1–S6 of
			planning/WG_Decision_Request_Single_500_Series_Archive.md). Ownership (S4): this is a
			series-wide artifact and belongs to NAS9300-500 or the 011–014 packaging parts, NOT to
			Part 520 — P520 conforms to it and provides the worked instance
			(SSPExamples/EVRangeExampleV3_AIP/lotar-500-manifest.xml). It sits in the p500#
			namespace (same chameleon pattern as P500_Series_Common.xsd, which it includes) for
			that reason.

			Archive layout this manifest describes (S1):

			  &lt;archive-root&gt;/
			    lotar-500-manifest.xml            this document
			    lotar-500-manifest.xml.xades      detached XAdES-LTA signature (mandatory CL3/CL4)
			    p510/&lt;object-id&gt;/P510_Manifest.xml  + requirements files
			    p520/&lt;object-id&gt;/P520_Manifest.xml  + the SSP/FMU package (internally unchanged)
			    p520/_decisions/&lt;guid&gt;.dtmd       canonical decision records of the baseline (S3)
			    p550/&lt;object-id&gt;/P550_Manifest.xml  link sets between the above
			    p5xx/...                          other 500-series parts, same pattern

			What the manifest carries, traced to the NAS9300-021 packaging requirements
			(gap-analyses/Requirements.md):
			  Package_Identifier (P1), Package_Type (P2), Package_Version (P11), Created_on /
			  Last_Modified_Date (P7/P8), Producer (P9, D4 enterprise id), Creating_Software (P5),
			  Submission_Agreement (P6), Retention (PD11), Baseline (NAS9300-500 §8.8.2, D4),
			  Contents/Entry (P3 structure, P4 content type, P13 file manifest, PD1 fixity, PD4 size,
			  D8 part reference), Decision_Records (PD17 approval records, S3), Schemas (GR1/GR3/
			  P14), Rights (P12, package-level only — S5), External_References (S6 layer 2: PD8/
			  D5/D6 relationships to OTHER archives, by identifier only), Signature (PD17/PD18).

			What it deliberately does NOT carry (S4b): semantic relationships between archived
			objects (requirement verifies scenario, model implements decision, ...). Those live in
			the P550 branch and in the part manifests' Traceability_Link elements; the top-level
			manifest records CONTAINMENT only, so there is one source of truth per relationship.

			Precedence (S5): a part manifest's GeneralPLMInfo is authoritative for its own object.
			The top-level manifest carries package-level information only (baseline, producer,
			package rights) and, per Entry, a COPY of the object's identifier and version for
			discovery — a contradiction between an Entry and its part manifest is a validation
			error (lotar-tools archive mode), never resolved in favour of the top-level document.

			METS mapping (S4): a normative mapping of every element below to METS 1.12 (mets/@OBJID,
			metsHdr, fileSec, structMap, mptr for External_References) is given in
			planning/P500_Archive_Manifest_METS_Mapping.md, so an archive can be exposed to
			preservation systems that speak METS without changing the 5xx readers' own format.

			Companion Schematron: lotar-p500-archive.sch (P500-ARCH-100..109). Filesystem checks
			(existence, fixity, cross-branch link resolution, decision-record copy consistency,
			Entry-vs-part-manifest consistency): lotar-tools `lotar check &lt;archive-root&gt;`.
		</xs:documentation>
	</xs:annotation>

	<!-- ===================================================================================
	     Root elements
	     =================================================================================== -->
	<xs:element name="Archive_Manifest" type="Archive_Manifest_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> Root element of lotar-500-manifest.xml — the top-level manifest of a
				500-series archive. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>

	<xs:element name="Baseline_Link_Set" type="Baseline_Link_Set_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> Root element of the link records of a metadata-only baseline link
				archive (S6 layer 3; the package type NAS9300-021 GR4 requires). The link archive is
				itself a 500-series archive with its own Archive_Manifest, whose single content
				Entry (@part="500", Content_Type="Other") points at this document. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:element>

	<!-- ===================================================================================
	     Archive manifest
	     =================================================================================== -->
	<xs:complexType name="Archive_Manifest_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Package_Identifier" type="LOTAR_Identifier_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Persistent identifier of this archive (P1): a LOTAR URN
						"urn:lotar:&lt;producer-code&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;" (producer code = CAGE or
						enterprise identifier, D4/P9; UUID = package identifier). Immutable, never
						reused; a new AIP version (P11) keeps the identifier and increments
						Package_Version. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Package_Type" type="Package_Type_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> OAIS package type (P2): SIP, AIP or DIP. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Package_Kind" type="Package_Kind_Type" minOccurs="0" default="content">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> "content" (default) for an archive holding 5xx content
						branches; "link" for a metadata-only baseline link archive (GR4, S6 layer 3)
						whose only content is a Baseline_Link_Set. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Package_Version" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> AIP version (P11), e.g. "1"; incremented on migration or
						preservation action. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Created_on" type="xs:dateTime">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package creation date (P7). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Last_Modified_Date" type="xs:dateTime" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Last modification date (P8). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Producer" type="Agent_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Producer organisation (P9), with its enterprise identifier
						(CAGE code, D4). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Creating_Software" type="Agent_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Software that created the package (P5): name and version. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Submission_Agreement" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Reference to the Submission Agreement between Producer and
						Archive (P6; required for a SIP). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Retention" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Planned retention period (PD11), e.g. "P50Y" or a policy
						reference. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Baseline" type="Baseline_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> The configured baseline this archive captures (NAS9300-500
						§8.8.2, NAS9300-002) and the product it belongs to (D4). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Contents" type="Contents_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Containment: one Entry per 500-series part artifact (P3, P13).
						Containment only — no semantic relationships here (S4b). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Decision_Records" type="Decision_Records_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> The canonical credible-decision-process records (.dtmd) of
						this baseline, one copy each under p520/_decisions/ (S3). Every other copy of
						the same record inside the archive (e.g. the one an SSP/FMU package carries
						internally for its own self-containment) must be byte-identical to the
						canonical one — checked by lotar-tools archive mode. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Schemas" type="Schemas_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Schemas and controlled vocabularies the archive's content
						conforms to (GR1, GR3, P14), by identifier and — when co-archived — by
						archive-relative path. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Rights" type="Rights_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package-level rights information (P12). Each part manifest's
						own GeneralPLMInfo rights fields remain authoritative for that object (S5);
						this block governs the package as a whole (e.g. the archive's export-control
						marking is the most restrictive marking of any part). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="External_References" type="External_References_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Declared outbound dependencies on OTHER archives (S6 layer 2;
						PD8, D5, D6): identifier of the foreign archive, its version, the relationship
						type, and the fixity of that archive's own top-level manifest at the time of
						linking, so the right archive version can be confirmed after migration. Never
						a locator: nothing that is a path or URL crosses an archive boundary. A dangling
						external reference is a warning at archive level and an error at repository
						level. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Signature" type="Signature_Reference_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Detached XAdES-LTA signature over this manifest (PD17/PD18).
						Because every Entry carries fixity, one signature over the manifest makes the
						whole archive tamper-evident. Mandatory at CL3/CL4, recommended at CL2
						(LOTAR_XAdES_LTA_Plan.md). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="schemaVersion" type="xs:string" use="required" fixed="0.1">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation> Version of this manifest schema the document conforms to. </xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="LOTAR_Identifier_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> LOTAR persistent identifier (S6 layer 1):
				urn:lotar:&lt;producer-code&gt;:&lt;archive-uuid&gt;[:&lt;object-id&gt;][#&lt;anchor&gt;].
				Lexical check only; semantics (immutability, version awareness) are in the clause text. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:anyURI">
			<xs:pattern value="urn:lotar:[A-Za-z0-9._\-]+:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}(:[^#\s/\\]+)?(#[^\s/\\]+)?"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Package_Type_Type">
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="SIP"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="AIP"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="DIP"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Package_Kind_Type">
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="content"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="link"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="Agent_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Name" type="xs:string"/>
			<xs:element name="Identifier" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Enterprise identifier (CAGE code, DUNS, ...) for an
						organisation; omitted for software. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Software version; omitted for an organisation. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Baseline_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Unique_baseline_id" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Same value as the part manifests' GeneralPLMInfo/
						Unique_baseline_id; a part manifest that names a different baseline is a
						validation error. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Baseline_Name" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Baseline_Status" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Status per the relevant domain part's vocabulary (D9), e.g.
						"frozen", "released". </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Product" type="Product_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Product/part identification the baseline belongs to (D4). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Product_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Part_Number" type="xs:string"/>
			<xs:element name="Part_Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Part_Description" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Program_Identifier" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="System_Identifier" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Contents_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Entry" type="Content_Entry_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Content_Entry_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> One archived 500-series object: which part governs it, what kind of
				content it is, its identifier and version (copied from its part manifest for
				discovery — the part manifest stays authoritative, S5), where its part manifest sits
				in the archive, and the fixity of that part manifest. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Content_Type" type="ContentTypeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> P4 content type, from P500_Series_Common.xsd's vocabulary
						(Requirement Model for 510, Behavioral Model for 520, Other for a 550 link set). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Unique_object_id" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> The object's identifier; must equal the part manifest's
						GeneralPLMInfo/Unique_object_id. Unique within the archive. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Version_identifier" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Must equal the part manifest's GeneralPLMInfo/Version_identifier. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Name" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Manifest_Path" type="xs:anyURI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Archive-root-relative locator of the part manifest
						(P510_Manifest.xml, P520_Manifest.xml, ...). Its first path segment is the
						part's branch folder "p&lt;part&gt;/" (S1). Everything under the manifest's
						own folder is that object's branch. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Fixity" type="Fixity_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Digest of the part manifest file (PD1). Fixity of the files the
						part manifest itself references is the part manifest's responsibility
						(P520_Related_Type/@checksum, SRMD, fmi-ls-ref, ...). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Size_bytes" type="xs:nonNegativeInteger">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Size of the part manifest file (PD4). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Format" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" default="application/xml">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> MIME type of the part manifest (PD2). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="part" type="Part_Number_Type" use="required">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation> NAS9300 500-series part number governing this entry (D8):
					510, 515, 520, 550, ..., or 500 for a series-level artifact such as a
					Baseline_Link_Set. </xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Part_Number_Type">
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:pattern value="5[0-9]{2}"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="Fixity_Type">
		<xs:simpleContent>
			<xs:extension base="Hex_Digest_Type">
				<xs:attribute name="algorithm" type="Digest_Algorithm_Type" use="required"/>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:simpleContent>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Hex_Digest_Type">
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:pattern value="[0-9a-fA-F]+"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Digest_Algorithm_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> Same algorithm names as fmi-ls-ref's TRelated/@checksumType and the
				SRMD @checksumType, so one resolver verifies all of them. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA-256"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA-384"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA-512"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA3-256"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA3-384"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHA3-512"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="Decision_Records_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Decision_Record" type="Decision_Record_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Decision_Record_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="GUID" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> The .dtmd's own GUID attribute; P520 manifests reference the
						record with Implements/Target_Id = "urn:uuid:&lt;GUID&gt;". </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Path" type="xs:anyURI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Archive-root-relative locator of the canonical copy:
						p520/_decisions/&lt;guid&gt;.dtmd (S3). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Fixity" type="Fixity_Type"/>
			<xs:element name="Size_bytes" type="xs:nonNegativeInteger" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Schemas_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Schema" type="Schema_Reference_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Schema_Reference_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Identifier" type="xs:anyURI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Namespace URI or vocabulary identifier (e.g.
						http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p520#, org.lotar-international.lotar-core.common). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Path" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Archive-root-relative locator when the schema/vocabulary is
						co-archived (GR1/GR3 "included or referenced"). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="kind" use="optional" default="schema">
			<xs:simpleType>
				<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
					<xs:enumeration value="schema"/>
					<xs:enumeration value="schematron"/>
					<xs:enumeration value="vocabulary"/>
				</xs:restriction>
			</xs:simpleType>
		</xs:attribute>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Rights_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Copyright" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="License" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Export_Controls" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Export_control_marking" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package-level marking — the most restrictive marking of any
						contained part. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Privacy_Rules" type="xs:anyURI" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Special_markings" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="External_References_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="External_Reference" type="External_Reference_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="External_Reference_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Target_Archive_Id" type="LOTAR_Identifier_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package_Identifier of the foreign archive
						(urn:lotar:&lt;producer&gt;:&lt;uuid&gt;), optionally extended with
						":&lt;object-id&gt;" when one object in it is meant. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Target_Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package_Version of the foreign archive the link was made
						against; absent = "latest in lineage". </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Target_Series" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> NAS9300 series/part of the foreign archive (100, 200, 400,
						500...), informative. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Relationship_Type" type="Relationship_Type_Type"/>
			<xs:element name="Relationship_SubType" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Local/extended vocabulary value when Relationship_Type is
						"Other" (GR3 extensibility, PD8 sub-type). </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Target_Manifest_Fixity" type="Fixity_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Digest of the foreign archive's own top-level manifest at the
						time of linking — the key to confirming, decades later, that the archive
						retrieved is the one meant. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Description" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp_PLM" type="xs:dateTime" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp_Archiving" type="xs:dateTime"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:simpleType name="Relationship_Type_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> Controlled relationship vocabulary (PD8/D5), in the style of PREMIS
				relationships and DCMI relation terms; extensible through "Other" +
				Relationship_SubType (GR3). </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="isDerivedFrom"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="verifies"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="validates"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="implements"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="isPartOfBaseline"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="supersedes"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="isSupersededBy"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="references"/>
			<xs:enumeration value="Other"/>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>

	<xs:complexType name="Signature_Reference_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Path" type="xs:anyURI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Archive-root-relative locator of the detached signature file,
						normally lotar-500-manifest.xml.xades. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Format" type="xs:string" default="XAdES-LTA" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Signer_Role" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>

	<!-- ===================================================================================
	     Baseline link set (metadata-only link archive, S6 layer 3)
	     =================================================================================== -->
	<xs:complexType name="Baseline_Link_Set_Type">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation> Signed, metadata-only set of relationships between archives of any
				series, produced by configuration management at baseline release. It is the one
				place bidirectional discovery is possible (an older CAD archive cannot know about a
				later simulation archive) and it is superseded, never edited, when a new baseline is
				cut. Both ends of every record are identifiers; nothing here is a locator. </xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Unique_baseline_id" type="xs:string"/>
			<xs:element name="Produced_by" type="Agent_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> The configuration-management role/organisation that cut the
						baseline. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Supersedes" type="LOTAR_Identifier_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Package_Identifier of the previous link archive of the same
						product lineage, if any. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Link_Record" type="Link_Record_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="schemaVersion" type="xs:string" use="required" fixed="0.1"/>
	</xs:complexType>

	<xs:complexType name="Link_Record_Type">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Source_Id" type="LOTAR_Identifier_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> urn:lotar:&lt;producer&gt;:&lt;archive-uuid&gt;[:&lt;object-id&gt;
						[#&lt;anchor&gt;]] — the archive and, optionally, the object the relation starts
						from. An anchor is resolved by that object's part manifest, never by this
						record. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source_Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Target_Id" type="LOTAR_Identifier_Type"/>
			<xs:element name="Target_Version" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Relationship_Type" type="Relationship_Type_Type"/>
			<xs:element name="Relationship_SubType" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Direction" minOccurs="0" default="directed">
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:enumeration value="directed"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="bidirectional"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source_Manifest_Fixity" type="Fixity_Type" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="Target_Manifest_Fixity" type="Fixity_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation> Digest of the target archive's top-level manifest at the time
						the record was made. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp_PLM" type="xs:dateTime"/>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp_Archiving" type="xs:dateTime"/>
			<xs:element name="Description" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
		</xs:sequence>
		<xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="optional"/>
	</xs:complexType>

</xs:schema>
